{
  "findings": [
    {
      "type": "checked_identity",
      "statement": "Under the stated uniform weak-composition law, for 0<h<R and 0<=a<=K, direct counting gives P(S_h=a | S_R=K) = binom(a+h-1,h-1) binom(K-a+R-h-1,R-h-1) / binom(K+R-1,R-1). The numerator independently counts compositions of a into h coordinates and K-a into R-h coordinates. Thus the supplied beta-binomial marginal identity is valid."
    },
    {
      "type": "checked_obstruction",
      "statement": "Low-state rarity cannot prove the claim. For fixed n with 2(4/9)^n<eta, the event Y_1=...=Y_(2n)=0 implies z_n=z_0(4/9)^n<eta because z_0<2. Its exact conditional probability is binom(K+R-2n-1,R-2n-1)/binom(K+R-1,R-1), which tends to (1+beta)^(-2n)>0 when K/R tends to beta. Hence entry into the low region has nonvanishing probability."
    },
    {
      "type": "review_conclusion",
      "statement": "No rigorous proof or actual accessible counterexample to XUB-MARKED-OCC follows from the supplied records. The exact one-block coefficient formula, even if accepted after direct composition counting, supplies only marginal probabilities. It gives no lower-tail or exponential-moment control for the number of marked blocks under the global endpoint constraint. Blocks are not conditionally independent, and a per-start union bound cannot supply the required Laplace estimate."
    },
    {
      "type": "logical_separation",
      "statement": "Even establishing occupation of bounded-positive non-low blocks would not prove the claim: resonant blocks are deleted from C_q. A separate joint estimate must show that amplified resonances cannot remove too many of the occupied blocks. Full multiplicative order modulo 3^Q does not provide the required discrepancy bound on the much shorter accessible exponent window."
    }
  ],
  "claim_status": "OPEN",
  "first_missing_step": {
    "name": "Non-low bounded-positive block occupation inequality",
    "inequality": "Let A_q be the event that every pair total in block q lies in {1,...,B_0} and the block entry satisfies z>=eta, with no resonance restriction. Prove that there exist C<infinity and R_0 such that, for every sufficiently large accessible R=2J+epsilon and every actual coupled array (r,R,tau,K) satisfying the frozen constraints, E[exp(-lambda * sum_{q in Q_R} 1_{A_q}) | S_R=K and the exact first-passage data] <= C/R.",
    "why_strictly_narrower": "Since C_q is a subset of A_q, sum_q 1_{A_q} >= sum_q 1_{C_q}, so exp(-lambda sum 1_{A_q}) <= exp(-lambda sum 1_{C_q}). Therefore the primary claim implies this inequality. It removes the short-orbit resonance arithmetic and isolates the first unresolved occupation problem.",
    "why_not_proved_by_displayed_reductions": "The beta-binomial formula controls one sampled height, and exact composition counts control one prescribed word. Neither controls the joint lower tail across a growing disjoint grid. Endpoint conditioning creates dependence, low visits have positive probability, and no proved cycle/ballot identity resolves the affine threshold, rational ties, even-time sampling, and odd singleton conventions. Moreover, proving this inequality alone would still not establish the primary claim because resonant deletion remains."
  },
  "unexpected_findings": [
    {
      "escalation_candidate": "The supplied documents do not specify the actual preregistered grid Q_R, the numerical symbolic-supply threshold, or the admissible range of c. Uniform constants and boundary blocks therefore cannot be audited from the supplied material. These data should be attached before a proof or counterexample can be fully checked."
    },
    {
      "escalation_candidate": "The phrase 'conditioned on the exact first-passage data' is not accompanied by a displayed derivation that this additional conditioning leaves the suffix law exactly uniform over weak compositions with total K. The frozen definitions assert that law, but any application outside this task needs the seam-conditioning identity stated explicitly."
    }
  ]
}
